.TH WELLCPU 1 "August 2026" "wellcpu 1.0" "wellutils"
.SH NAME
Wellcpu \- CPU overview: model, topology, caches, per-core load and frequencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wellcpu
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wellcpu
.PP
Reports the processor: model name, architecture, socket/core/thread
topology, base and maximum frequencies, cache hierarchy (L1d/L1i/L2/L3),
notable instruction-set features (AVX, AVX2, AVX-512, AES, ...),
virtualization support, hypervisor detection and the current cpufreq
governor. A second section shows live per-core utilization with a load
bar and the current per-core frequency read from sysfs.
.PP
When stdout is a terminal the output is drawn as a box; when piped a plain layout is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en|auto"
Force report language (default \fBauto\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Force, disable, or auto-detect ANSI colour.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Plain text output without box drawing.
.TP
.B \-\-box
Force box drawing even when piped.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emoji icons.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable JSON on stdout; errors still go to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose tracing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line usage.
.TP
.B 3
Unexpected runtime error.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WELLUTILS_LANG
\fBru\fR or \fBen\fR; overrides locale detection.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colour in auto mode.
.SH AUTHOR
wellbou_
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wellutils (1), .BR wellgpu (1), .BR wellblock (1)
